# Edge Cases — Pharmacy Benefit Checker (Sprint 14)
### Scenarios a Standard Test Suite Would Miss

---

## EC-01 | Concurrent Sessions — Same Member, Two Devices

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-01 |
| **Scenario** | A member is logged into the Pharmacy Benefit Checker on a desktop browser at home AND simultaneously on a work laptop. They search for the same drug on both devices within seconds of each other |
| **Why Risky** | If session management isn't properly isolated, one session could receive the other's results, or a plan type change triggered mid-session could cause one device to show stale plan data while the other shows updated data. In a healthcare context, a member acting on wrong formulary data could make incorrect medication decisions |
| **Expected Behavior** | Both sessions operate independently and return identical, correct results for the same member. No cross-session data bleed. If one session is invalidated (e.g., security policy allows only one active session), the older session receives a clear "session ended" message — not a silent failure |
| **Likelihood** | 🟡 Medium |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

