## EC-02 | Brand Name vs Generic Drug Search — Different Results

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-02 |
| **Scenario** | A member searches for "Lipitor" (brand name) — the formulary only contains "Atorvastatin" (the generic equivalent). The system must decide: return the generic match, return no result, or prompt the member |
| **Why Risky** | If the system returns "Requires Further Review" or "Not Covered" for "Lipitor" when the generic IS covered, the member may believe their medication is not covered and either skip it or pay out of pocket unnecessarily. This is both a member experience failure and a potential liability issue |
| **Expected Behavior** | System either: (a) maps brand name to generic and returns the generic's formulary status with a note ("Showing results for Atorvastatin, the generic equivalent of Lipitor"), OR (b) returns no match and prompts the member to search by generic name. It must NOT return "Not Covered" if the generic equivalent is covered |
| **Likelihood** | 🔴 High |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

