## EC-03 | Drug Name Misspelling — Fuzzy Match or Hard Fail

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-03 |
| **Scenario** | Member types "Metfromin" instead of "Metformin" — a common misspelling of a widely used diabetes medication. The formulary API performs an exact string match and returns no result |
| **Why Risky** | Members are not clinical professionals — misspellings are expected and frequent, especially on mobile. If the system returns "Requires Review" or a no-result state for every minor misspelling, members lose trust in the tool and call the member helpline instead, increasing operational cost. More critically, a member may assume a drug is not covered because of a typo |
| **Expected Behavior** | System either: (a) performs fuzzy matching and returns the closest formulary match with a note ("Did you mean: Metformin?"), OR (b) clearly indicates no exact match was found and suggests correcting the spelling. It must NOT silently return "Not Covered" for a misspelled drug name |
| **Likelihood** | 🔴 High |
| **Impact** | 🟡 Medium |

