## EC-04 | Recent Plan Change — Which Formulary Is Applied?

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-04 |
| **Scenario** | A member switched from PPO Select (batch-cache plan) to a standard real-time plan effective today. They log in and search for a drug. The system must determine which plan's formulary to use — the old plan or the new one |
| **Why Risky** | This is one of the highest-risk data integrity scenarios in healthcare systems. If the system applies the old plan's formulary (possibly from last night's batch cache), the member sees coverage information that no longer applies to them. They could go to a pharmacy expecting a Tier 2 copay and discover they are now on a different plan with a different tier structure — causing financial surprise and eroding trust |
| **Expected Behavior** | System applies the formulary of the member's current active plan as of today's effective date. If plan change processing has a lag, system displays a message: "Your plan was recently updated. Results shown reflect your new plan. If you believe this is incorrect, please contact member services." No residual batch-cache data from the old plan is served |
| **Likelihood** | 🟡 Medium |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

