## EC-06 | Mobile Browser Access — Degraded but Safe Experience

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-06 |
| **Scenario** | Despite mobile being out of scope for Sprint 14, 61% of portal sessions are on mobile (per James's email). A member accesses the Pharmacy Benefit Checker on a mobile browser — the feature loads but renders in an unoptimized desktop layout |
| **Why Risky** | Two distinct risks: (1) **Safety risk** — if the ACA disclaimer or last-updated timestamp is pushed off-screen or hidden on a small viewport, the member never sees it. This is a compliance failure even though mobile is "out of scope." (2) **Data risk** — if the mobile browser triggers partial page loads or truncated API responses, a member could see an incomplete result and make a healthcare decision based on it |
| **Expected Behavior** | Even in the unoptimized mobile experience: (a) ACA disclaimer must be fully visible without horizontal scrolling, (b) last-updated timestamp must render for batch-cache plan members, (c) authentication gate must still function, (d) "Requires Review" messaging must appear correctly. The feature may look unpolished on mobile — but it must never be unsafe |
| **Likelihood** | 🔴 High — 61% mobile traffic makes this near-certain |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

