## EC-07 | Screen Reader Compatibility — Section 508 Accessibility

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-07 |
| **Scenario** | A visually impaired member uses a screen reader (JAWS or NVDA) to navigate the Pharmacy Benefit Checker. They search for a drug and try to interpret the results — coverage status, tier, copay indicator, ACA disclaimer, and timestamp |
| **Why Risky** | Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act requires federal healthcare systems to be accessible. Carelon, operating in the ACA/federal healthcare space, is likely subject to this requirement. If formulary results are rendered as untagged divs, icons without alt text, or dynamic content that screen readers cannot detect, a visually impaired member cannot access the same benefit information as a sighted member — which is both a legal risk and an equity issue |
| **Expected Behavior** | All result fields must have proper ARIA labels. Coverage status, tier, copay, and disclaimer text must be announced by screen reader in a logical reading order. Dynamic result loading must trigger an ARIA live region update so the screen reader announces new content without requiring the member to manually navigate to it. The ACA disclaimer must be read aloud — not skipped |
| **Likelihood** | 🟡 Medium |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

