## EC-08 | Partial Drug Name / Wildcard-Style Search

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | EC-08 |
| **Scenario** | Member types only "met" — a partial drug name — and submits. The formulary contains multiple drugs beginning with "met" (Metformin, Metoprolol, Methylprednisolone). It is undefined in the AC whether partial search is supported |
| **Why Risky** | If partial search is not handled, the system returns an unexpected result (wrong drug's formulary data) or a no-match error that confuses the member. If partial search IS supported but not bounded, the API could return hundreds of matches, causing performance degradation or an unusable results list. Neither behavior is defined in any AC — this is a pure gap |
| **Expected Behavior** | System either: (a) requires a minimum character threshold (e.g., 3+ characters) and returns a bounded list of matching drug names for the member to select from, OR (b) requires full drug name entry and displays inline guidance. Results must never auto-select a drug without member confirmation. A partial match must never show formulary data for the wrong drug |
| **Likelihood** | 🔴 High — natural member behavior |
| **Impact** | 🔴 High |

